count for `TAB` stops.  The terminal dimensions can be found with `stty -a` or c
heck the `TERM` definition (see `/usr/share/misc/terminfo`) or both.

Curses library supports the environment variables `TERM`, `LINES`, and `COLUMNS`
.  It possible to temporarily set `LINES` or `COLUMNS` or both smaller than the
terminal window size for easier testing and debugging, eg.

    $ LINES=10 ./ae file

